---
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const url = "https://api.eyes.pictures/w/location";
---

<Layout
  title="Send my spot automatically"
  ogTitle="Eyes: send your spot automatically"
  description="Set up iPhone automations that send your spot to Eyes by themselves."
  noindex
>
  <h1 class="ui-h1">Send my spot automatically</h1>
  <p class="ui-notice ui-notice--success">Have the Eyes app? You don't need this.</p>
  <p class="ui-text-secondary">
    Your iPhone sends your spot to Eyes by itself: once a day, and when Eyes asks because a paid task is near. About
    10 minutes, once. Needs iOS 26 or later.
  </p>
  <p class="ui-notice">
    <Icon name="message" /> Text AUTO to the Eyes number first. Eyes texts you a code; you paste it in step 4.
  </p>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">1. Make automation A: every morning</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open Shortcuts, tap Automation, then <b>+</b>.</li>
      <li>Choose Time of Day, set 9:00 AM and Daily, choose <b>Run Immediately</b>, tap Next.</li>
      <li>Tap New Blank Automation, then do steps 2 to 4 below.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">2. Add Get Current Location</h2>
    <p>Search the actions for "Get Current Location" and tap it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">3. Add Get Contents of URL</h2>
    <p>Search for "Get Contents of URL", tap it, tap the URL field and paste:</p>
    <button type="button" class="ui-button ui-button--block" data-copy={url}>Copy URL</button>
    <p>Tap the arrow to show more. Set Method to <b>POST</b>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">4. Add the header and body</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Headers: Add new header. Key:
        <button type="button" class="ui-button" data-copy="Authorization">Copy key</button>
        Value: paste <b>Bearer </b> then your code, with one space between.
        <button type="button" class="ui-button" data-copy="Bearer ">Copy "Bearer "</button>
      </li>
      <li>Request Body: JSON. Add three Text fields:</li>
    </ol>
    <dl class="ui-kv">
      <dt>lat</dt>
      <dd>tap the value, choose Current Location, then Latitude</dd>
      <dt>lng</dt>
      <dd>Current Location, then Longitude</dd>
      <dt>source</dt>
      <dd>
        shortcut <button type="button" class="ui-button" data-copy="shortcut">Copy</button>
      </dd>
    </dl>
    <p>Tap Done. Automation A is on.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">5. Make automation B: when Eyes asks</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Automation, <b>+</b>, Message. Sender: the Eyes number. Message Contains:</li>
    </ol>
    <button type="button" class="ui-button ui-button--block" data-copy="Eyes ping">Copy "Eyes ping"</button>
    <ol start="2">
      <li>Choose Run Immediately, tap Next, New Blank Automation.</li>
      <li>Repeat steps 2 to 4, and add a fourth field: <b>input</b>, value Shortcut Input.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">Optional: when you head out</h2>
    <p>Make one more with Charger, Is Disconnected, Run Immediately, and the same steps 2 to 4.</p>
  </section>

  <p id="copied" class="ui-notice ui-notice--success" role="status" hidden></p>
  <p class="ui-field__hint">
    iOS 27: make one shortcut with steps 2 to 4, then Edit, Automation, and add each trigger there. Text STOP to
    delete your spot and turn every code off.
  </p>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { $ } from "../api.ts";
  import { wireCopy } from "../automation.ts";

  wireCopy(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]"), $("copied"), (text) =>
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text),
  );
</script>
